# Eigen Project Rules and Guidelines

## Development Environment
- Please don't run terminal commands to install packages yourself. Ask me to do it (output the command and instructions as text)
- Use Bun as the JavaScript runtime for both server and client development
- All development should be done with TypeScript for type safety

## Project Overview
- This is a Google Workspace-like application with multiple integrated apps (Mail, Drive, Docs, Stickies, Calendar, Contacts, Space, Admin, Index, Setup)
- The project follows a monorepo structure with:
  - /apps: Contains all applications (frontend and API server)
  - /packages: Shared libraries and UI components
  - /packages/ui: Reusable UI components
  - /packages/lib: Shared business logic

## Technical Stack
- Backend: Bun + Elysia for server routes + Drizzle ORM for database
- Frontend: React (with Bun) + TypeScript
- Data Management: TanStack Query for data fetching and caching
- Routing: TanStack Router for type-safe routing
- UI: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui components
- Authentication: better-auth for user authentication and session management

## Code Style & Conventions
- ALWAYS USE ENGLISH in all code and all texts you generate
- Prefer a simple and clean implementation. Keep code simple and HTML layout clean and simple
- Use shadcn defaults for UI components
- Follow established naming conventions:
  - For routes: Use domain-based naming (e.g., mail, drive, contacts)
  - For functions: Use camelCase and descriptive naming
  - For components: Use PascalCase

## Types & Interfaces
- Always use `type` instead of `interface`, except when methods are involved
- All types must be defined in `packages/lib/src/types/[domain].ts`
- Import types from `@workspace/lib/types/[domain]` or `@workspace/lib/types`
- Before creating a new type, check if it already exists in the types folder
- Always discuss with the user before adding, creating, or modifying types

## Architecture Patterns
- API Routes: Group by domain in /apps/api/src/routes
- Frontend Apps: Place in separate directories under /apps
- Shared Logic: Extract to /packages/lib
- UI Components: Place reusable components in /packages/ui
- Authentication: All protected routes should include the auth: true property
- Hooks: Place in `packages/lib/src/lib/[domain]/hooks/use-[name].ts`
- Backend Domain Classes: Business logic in `apps/api/src/lib/[domain]/[domain].ts`, accessed via `Home` singleton (see `apps/api/src/lib/home/home.ts`)

## Real-Time Updates (SSE)
- Use Server-Sent Events for real-time cache invalidation across tabs/devices
- SSE handlers are in `packages/lib/src/lib/[domain]/sse-handlers.ts`
- SSE event builders are in `apps/api/src/lib/[domain]/sse-events.ts`
- Create dedicated invalidate functions in hooks files and call them from both:
  - SSE handlers (for cross-tab sync)
  - Mutation onSuccess callbacks (for optimistic updates)

## API Client
- Use Treaty client from `packages/lib/src/lib/api.ts` for type-safe API calls (exports `driveApi`, `mailApi`, `contactsApi`, etc.)
- API clients are generated from Elysia route types

## Query Key Patterns
- Define query keys as objects (e.g., `driveKeys`, `emailKeys`, `contactKeys`)
- Use consistent key structure: `[domain, 'list'|'detail', ...params]`
- Export invalidation functions alongside hooks for reuse

## Module Exports
- Each domain module has an `index.ts` that re-exports public API
- Import from `@workspace/lib/[domain]` not deep paths

## File Types
- Docs use mimeType `application/eigendoc` (`.eigendoc` extension)
- Stickies use mimeType `application/eigenstickies` (`.eigenstickies` extension)
- URL params use hyphens (`application-eigendoc`), database uses slashes

## Development Workflow
- Use bun scripts defined in root package.json for development:
  - serve: Run all applications
  - serve:[appname]: Run specific app with API server
  - typecheck: Run TypeScript type check across all packages and apps (`bun run typecheck`)
- Run `bun run typecheck` after making changes to verify type safety across the monorepo
- Always update types when changing database schemas
- Remember to invalidate queries when mutating data
- Create custom hooks for reusable data fetching logic

## State Management
- Use TanStack Query for server state
- Use React state hooks for local UI state
- Use appropriate caching strategies for optimizing performance

## Documentation
- Keep code comments minimal - code should be self-documenting:
  - DO NOT use JSDoc style comments
  - Only add comments to explain complex business logic that isn't immediately clear
  - Focus on making the code readable rather than relying on comments
  - Use clear variable and function names instead of comments where possible
- Keep the README updated with setup instructions and project overview